{
  "name": "Generate missing WordPress image alt text with OpenAI vision",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b24b4315-4105-5b0a-b802-191455eddf63",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -200,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## Generate missing WordPress image alt text with OpenAI vision\n\nFinds images in your WordPress media library that have no alt text, asks OpenAI to describe each one in a short sentence, checks the result, and saves it back through the WordPress REST API.\n\n**Dry run is ON by default.** Nothing is written to WordPress until you set `dryRun` to false in the Config node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6bba4b97-d3fc-5678-a830-2ea66e1cc28b",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        300,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## Setup\n\n1. In WordPress, create an Application Password (Users > Profile) for a user who can edit media.\n2. In n8n, create a **Basic Auth** credential: username = your WordPress username, password = the Application Password. Select it in the two WordPress HTTP nodes.\n3. Add an **OpenAI** credential and select it in the OpenAI node.\n4. Open the Config node and set `siteUrl` (no trailing slash), limits, language and model.\n5. Run once with `dryRun` = true and review the output.\n6. Set `dryRun` = false to save alt text.\n\nYour site must be public so OpenAI can fetch the image URLs. Use HTTPS for Application Passwords."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1db25368-960d-5ed9-bcac-2853ea2e531e",
      "name": "Branches",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        860,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## What each branch does\n\n- **Valid + dry run:** shows the proposed alt text only.\n- **Valid + live:** updates the image in WordPress.\n- **Not valid:** skipped (empty, unreadable, or longer than `maxAltLength`).\n\nOpenAI and update calls continue on error, so one failed image does not stop the run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "217ee2a3-8c1d-52f2-8de9-a3ce749698d6",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
        -200,
        460
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
